GUIDES={
 'guiding.html':(1,'Why does light stay inside a tiny strip of glass or silicon?','Light is trapped by total internal reflection in a high-index core. As a wave, it can only travel in a few stable patterns, the modes.',
   ['Find the critical angle for silicon against glass in step 1.','In step 3, make the core thinner until only mode 0 is left.','In step 4, compare bend losses for high and low index contrast.'],'nothing: this is the starting point'),
 'modes-2d.html':(1,'What do the modes of a wire waveguide look like?','Wire waveguides, the standard on photonic chips, confine light sideways and vertically. Their modes come in two polarizations, TE and TM, with different speeds.',
   ['Load "Square Si 300 × 300" and compare the TE0 and TM0 indices.','In the SiN preset, superpose TE0 with TE1 and watch the light swing from side to side.','Press "Sweep width" and find the widest single-mode silicon wire.'],'what a mode and the effective index are (step 3 of How Light Is Guided)'),
 'components.html':(2,'How do you split, combine and filter light on a chip?','Classic components use simple physics: evanescent coupling, symmetry, multimode interference and resonance.',
   ['Find the coupler length that gives a 50:50 split.','Measure the ring spectrum, then tap a dip to see light pile up inside the ring.','In the grating coupler, find the fiber angle that couples the most light.'],'evanescent tails and modes (chapter 1)'),
 'circuit-lab.html':(7,'How do components work together as a spectrometer, a sensor or a switch?','A circuit is components connected by waveguides. Each component is described by a small table of numbers, so a whole circuit can be solved instantly at every wavelength.',
   ['In the spectrometer, feed in the unknown sample and see which channels light up.','In the biosensor, find how many bound molecules give half the full signal.','Build an interferometer yourself: a Y-splitter, two waveguides of different length, and a coupler.'],'directional couplers and rings (Component Workshop)'),
 'inverse-design-2d.html':(3,'What if a computer designed the component instead?','Inverse design starts from the goal. Gradients from just two simulations tell every pixel how to change.',
   ['Optimize the bend, then switch the design view to Gradient.','Raise the minimum feature size and see what it costs in efficiency.','Run the mode sorter and flip between the TE0 and TE1 inputs.'],'the idea of the adjoint method (How Inverse Design Works)'),
 'how-inverse-design-works.html':(3,'How can an optimizer know how to change thousands of pixels at once?','One forward and one adjoint simulation give the gradient for every pixel. Linearity, locality and reciprocity make it exact.',
   ['Tap a few pixels by brute force, then compare them with the adjoint gradient map.','Press "Check 5 pixels against brute force" and look at the differences.','Run the loop and watch the forward and adjoint fields become identical.'],'modes and waveguides (chapters 1 and 2), and a little linear algebra for step 6'),
 'metalens.html':(7,'Can a flat layer, thinner than a micrometre, focus light like a lens?','The optimizer only asks for bright light at one point. The lens phase profile emerges by itself.',
   ['Compare the dots on the phase plot with the ideal hyperbolic line.','Shorten the focal length: the numerical aperture rises and the spot shrinks.','Try "Two foci", a function no single classic lens can do.'],'the idea of inverse design (Inverse Design 2D)'),
 'gc-opt.html':(3,'Can an optimizer beat a hand-designed grating coupler?','A uniform grating emits a lopsided beam. By changing every trench, the optimizer reshapes the beam to match the fiber, guided by one adjoint simulation per step.',
   ['Run the optimizer and compare with the uniform grating line.','Watch the trench pattern: where do trenches get narrower or wider?','Press "Compare spectra" and check whether the gain holds across wavelengths.'],'the grating coupler in the Component Workshop'),
 'design-studio.html':(3,'What would you build if you set up the problem yourself?','Every inverse-design problem has the same ingredients: sources, a design region, detectors, and a figure of merit that says what "good" means.',
   ['Load the bend, move the output waveguide to the top, and re-optimize.','Add a flux monitor on a leak path and give it a "minimize" term.','Build a TE0 to TE1 converter from scratch in the blank scene.'],'chapters 1 and 2, and How Inverse Design Works'),
 'photonic-computing.html':(6,'Can light do the math of a neural network?','A mesh of tunable interferometers multiplies light by a matrix as it passes. Its phases are the weights, so the chip can be trained.',
   ['Set θ in step 1 so that all light leaves at the bottom.','Program "Reverse order", then add a coupler error and watch the match drop.','Train the network, then paint a pattern it has never seen.'],'nothing beyond chapter 2; directional couplers help'),
 'paint-chip.html':(6,'Can you beat the computer at designing a photonic chip?','Light is a wave: smooth curves and tapers guide it, sharp corners scatter it. An optimizer can start from your drawing and improve it.',
   ['Get three stars on "Turn the corner" by hand.','Paint a Y-splitter in "Fair split" with the mirror on, then let the optimizer improve it.','In "Color sorter", compare "Optimize my drawing" with "Optimize from scratch".'],'nothing. Chapter 1 explains why your designs work'),
}
def chof(f): return GUIDES[f][0]
TOOLS=[p for p in PAGES if chof(p[0])!=6]
def guide(f,i):
    ch,q,key,tries,pre=GUIDES[f]
    li=''.join(f'<li>{t}</li>' for t in tries)
    num='EXTRA' if ch==6 else f'TOOL {[p[0] for p in TOOLS].index(f)+1} OF {len(TOOLS)}'
    return (f'<section class="ipp-guide" aria-label="About this tool"><div class="ipp-gtop"><span>{CH[ch].upper()}</span><span>{num}</span></div>'
            f'<div><p class="ipp-q">{q}</p><p class="ipp-key"><b>Key idea:</b> {key}</p><p class="ipp-key"><b>You need:</b> {pre}</p></div>'
            f'<details class="ipp-try" open><summary>Three things to try</summary><ol>{li}</ol></details></section>'
            "<script>try{if(matchMedia('(max-width:760px)').matches)document.querySelector('.ipp-try').removeAttribute('open');}catch(e){}</script>")
def nav(cur):
    curch=chof(cur) if cur in GUIDES else 0
    chs=''
    for c in sorted(CHNAV):
        first=[p for p in PAGES if chof(p[0])==c][0][0]
        lab=(f'<b>{c}</b>' if c<6 else '<b>+</b>')+CHNAV[c]
        chs+=f'<a href="{first}"{" aria-current=\"true\"" if c==curch else ""}>{lab}</a>'
    mine=[p for p in PAGES if chof(p[0])==curch]
    sub=''
    if len(mine)>1:
        sub='<div class="ipp-sub" aria-label="Tools in this chapter">'+''.join(f'<a href="{f}"{" aria-current=\"page\"" if f==cur else ""}>{name}</a>' for f,_,_,name in mine)+'</div>'
    return f'<nav class="ipp-nav" aria-label="Photonics Playground"><a class="ipp-brand" href="index.html">'+LOGO+f'Photonics Playground</a><div class="ipp-chs">{chs}</div>{sub}</nav>'
def nextnav(i):
    prev=PAGES[i-1] if i>0 else None; nxt=PAGES[i+1] if i<len(PAGES)-1 else None
    l=f'<a href="{prev[0]}"><span>Previous</span>← {prev[3]}</a>' if prev else '<a href="index.html"><span>Overview</span>← All tools</a>'
    r=f'<a href="{nxt[0]}" style="text-align:right"><span>Next</span>{nxt[3]} →</a>' if nxt else '<a href="index.html" style="text-align:right"><span>Overview</span>All tools →</a>'
    return f'<nav class="ipp-next" aria-label="Previous and next tool">{l}{r}</nav>'
BASE='''<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<style>:root{color-scheme:light;padding-top:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px);padding-bottom:env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)}body{margin:0;font:14px system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",sans-serif}img{max-width:100%}[hidden]{display:none!important}</style>
'''
os.makedirs(OUT,exist_ok=True)
for old in ['slab.html','inverse-design-1d.html']:
    if os.path.exists(OUT+old): os.remove(OUT+old)
for i,(out,src,short,name) in enumerate(PAGES):
    s=open(SRC+'pages/'+src).read()
    k=s.index('<div class="wrap">')
    head,body=s[:k],s[k:]
    head=head.replace('</style>',NAVCSS+FOOTCSS+'</style>',1)+'<link rel="icon" href="'+FAV+'">'
    body=body.replace('<div class="wrap">','<div class="wrap">\n  '+nav(out),1)
    assert '</header>' in body,out
    body=body.replace('<span class="kicker">PHOTONICS PLAYGROUND</span>','')
    # previous/next at the end of the main column
    j=body.index('<script')
    endwrap=body.rfind('</div>',0,j)
    body=body[:endwrap]+'  '+nextnav(i)+'\n  '+FOOT+'\n'+body[endwrap:]
    body=body.replace('</header>','</header>\n  '+guide(out,i),1)
    if out in TOURS:
        head=head.replace('</style>',TOURCSS+'</style>',1)
        body=body+TOURJS.replace('__STEPS__',json.dumps(TOURS[out],ensure_ascii=False))
    open(OUT+out,'w').write(BASE+head+'</head>\n<body>\n'+body+'\n</body></html>\n')
h=open(SRC+'hub-index.html').read().replace('</head>','<link rel="icon" href="'+FAV+'"></head>',1).replace('/*NAV*/',NAVCSS+FOOTCSS).replace('  </section>\n</div>\n\n<script>','  </section>\n  '+FOOT+'\n</div>\n\n<script>',1).replace('<!--NAVBAR-->',nav('index.html'))
for key in ['guiding','modes','components','id2d','gcopt','studio','adjoint']:
    h=h.replace(f'__T:{key}__',f'<img class="l" src="thumbs/{key}-light.webp" alt=""><img class="d" src="thumbs/{key}-dark.webp" alt="">')
open(OUT+'index.html','w').write(h)


